{
  "title": "Three reads, one plan",
  "host": "main--site--org.aem.page",
  "brand": {
    "dark": "#1d2a3a",
    "dark2": "#2c3e55",
    "accent": "#f2a33a"
  },
  "voice": {
    "provider": "say",
    "sayVoice": "Samantha",
    "sayRate": 200,
    "final": {
      "provider": "elevenlabs",
      "voiceId": "[voice id]",
      "model": "eleven_multilingual_v2",
      "settings": {
        "stability": 0.42,
        "similarity_boost": 0.75,
        "style": 0.35,
        "use_speaker_boost": true,
        "speed": 1.1
      }
    }
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "title",
      "duration": 4,
      "kicker": "Example Group · Brand Visibility",
      "title": "Three reads.<br><em>One plan.</em>",
      "sub": "A way to think about search, AI answers and the website as one thing"
    },
    {
      "id": "situation",
      "type": "stats",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Example Group today",
      "stats": [
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "[a fact from the annual report]"
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "[a second]"
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "[a third]"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "[Who the firm is, in one sentence.] {s1}[Fact.] {s2}[Fact.] {s3}[Fact.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "brands",
      "type": "brands",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Three websites today",
      "cards": [
        {
          "page": "old-group",
          "name": "Example Group",
          "domain": "example.com"
        },
        {
          "page": "old-shop",
          "name": "Shop",
          "domain": "example-shop.com",
          "now": "[new name, if renamed]"
        },
        {
          "page": "old-pro",
          "name": "Professional",
          "domain": "example-pro.com"
        }
      ],
      "one": "Example",
      "lines": [
        "Shop<small>Example Shop</small>",
        "Professional<small>Example Pro</small>"
      ],
      "narration": "[Its sites today.] {renamed}[What was renamed.] {merge}[What it is becoming.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "define",
      "type": "pillars",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Brand visibility: three reads of the same firm",
      "cols": [
        {
          "at": "arrive",
          "h": "Read 1",
          "k": "Who arrives",
          "items": [
            "What visitors come for, on every site",
            "Measured on the sites themselves",
            "The audience the firm already has"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "ask",
          "h": "Read 2",
          "k": "What people ask",
          "items": [
            "Questions put to search and AI assistants",
            "Who gets named in the answer",
            "The audience the firm could have"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "want",
          "h": "Read 3",
          "k": "What the firm wants",
          "items": [
            "Its own stated strategy",
            "Where growth should come from",
            "The audience it is aiming for"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "narration": "So what is brand visibility? Not a set of channels. Three reads of the same firm. {arrive}Who arrives. {ask}What people ask. {want}And what the firm wants."
    },
    {
      "id": "arrive",
      "type": "stats",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Read 1 · who arrives",
      "stats": [
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "n": "[meta.visits]",
          "t": "visits in [period], across the sites"
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "n": "[share]",
          "t": "land on a page about a client theme"
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "themes get visitors from more than one site"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "Read one: who arrives. {s1}[Visits.] {s2}[Share with a theme.] {s3}[Shared themes.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "space",
      "type": "space",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Read 2 · what people ask, and who is named",
      "sub": "[scope of reads.json] · compared with [the competitors, by name] only",
      "all": "Everything people ask AI assistants (not to scale)",
      "out": [
        "Left out: [what theme-rules exclude]"
      ],
      "addr": "Addressable for the firm",
      "addrSmall": "[topics] topics · [prompts] prompts a month",
      "segs": [
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "v": 40,
          "text": "40%",
          "label": "The firm leads",
          "small": "[prompts] a month",
          "play": "Defend",
          "playSmall": "make thin leads deep",
          "playAt": "plays"
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "v": 20,
          "text": "20%",
          "label": "A competitor leads",
          "small": "[prompts] a month",
          "play": "Win",
          "playSmall": "publish what the firm knows",
          "playAt": "plays"
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "v": 40,
          "text": "40%",
          "label": "Open, or thin",
          "small": "[prompts] a month",
          "play": "Claim",
          "playSmall": "be the first complete answer",
          "playAt": "plays"
        }
      ],
      "stepsLabel": "Track it",
      "steps": [
        "Topics owned",
        "Mentions",
        "Citations",
        "Visits",
        "Leads"
      ],
      "narration": "Read two: what people ask. {all}[The whole space.] {addr}[The part that matters to the firm.] {s1}[Where it leads.] {s2}[Where others lead.] {s3}[What is open.] {plays}Three states, three jobs. {track}[One line to track them.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "fetch",
      "type": "bars",
      "cls": "tight",
      "hold": 0.4,
      "title": "Optional read · what assistants fetch",
      "sub": "Citation attempts on [site] pages · [window] · [what is not tracked]",
      "rows": [
        {
          "at": "b1",
          "label": "[theme]",
          "v": 80,
          "text": "80"
        },
        {
          "at": "b2",
          "label": "[theme]",
          "v": 60,
          "text": "60"
        },
        {
          "at": "lo",
          "label": "[theme the firm wants]",
          "small": "[why it matters]",
          "v": 5,
          "text": "5"
        }
      ],
      "foot": "[total attempts in the window, and where most of them go]",
      "narration": "[What a citation attempt is, in one sentence.] {b1}[What is read most.] {b2}[The surprise.] {lo}[What the firm wants and assistants do not open.] {foot}[The total.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "wants",
      "type": "pillars",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Read 3 · what the firm wants",
      "cols": [
        {
          "at": "c1",
          "h": "Brand",
          "k": "[e.g. one brand]",
          "items": [
            "[statement, with date]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "c2",
          "h": "Growth",
          "k": "[where from]",
          "items": [
            "[statement, with date]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "c3",
          "h": "Focus",
          "k": "[n] named growth areas",
          "items": [
            "[area]",
            "[area]",
            "[area]"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "narration": "Read three: what the firm wants, read from what it says in public. {c1}[Brand.] {c2}[Growth.] {c3}[Named growth areas.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "reads",
      "type": "browser",
      "hold": 0.6,
      "pages": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "page": "reads-arrive",
          "url": " · three reads, one plan",
          "label": "<b>Read 1</b> who arrives, by client theme"
        },
        {
          "at": "ask",
          "page": "reads-ask",
          "url": " · three reads, one plan",
          "label": "<b>Read 2</b> what people ask AI"
        },
        {
          "at": "want",
          "page": "reads-want",
          "url": " · three reads, one plan",
          "label": "<b>Read 3</b> what the firm wants"
        },
        {
          "at": "plan",
          "page": "reads-plan",
          "url": " · three reads, one plan",
          "label": "<b>One plan</b> a job for each theme"
        }
      ],
      "scroll": [
        {
          "at": 0.3,
          "to": "chart",
          "dur": 2.5
        }
      ],
      "rings": [
        {
          "at": "t1",
          "until": "t2",
          "mark": "reads-plan.ai"
        },
        {
          "at": "t2",
          "until": "t3",
          "mark": "reads-plan.health"
        },
        {
          "at": "t3",
          "mark": "reads-plan.people"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "Now merge them, by what a client is trying to solve. [Read one, by theme.] {ask}[Read two joins.] {want}[Read three joins.] {plan}And each theme gets a job. {t1}[Claim.] {t2}[Defend.] {t3}[Win.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "p-claim",
      "type": "title",
      "duration": 3,
      "kicker": "Job 1 of 3",
      "title": "Claim what's <em>open</em>",
      "sub": "[theme]: [why the three reads put it first]"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-how",
      "type": "browser",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "page": "theme-page",
          "url": "/themes/ai-and-data",
          "label": "<b>One possible answer</b> a theme, as one firm"
        }
      ],
      "scroll": [
        {
          "at": 0.3,
          "to": "row",
          "dur": 2.5
        }
      ],
      "rings": [
        {
          "at": "ring",
          "mark": "theme-page.row"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "[The theme, the visitors it has, what is missing.] {ring}[What the page does.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "p-defend",
      "type": "title",
      "duration": 3,
      "kicker": "Job 2 of 3",
      "title": "Defend what the firm <em>leads</em>",
      "sub": "[theme]: [why]"
    },
    {
      "id": "defend",
      "type": "bars",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "[theme]: [the finding]",
      "sub": "Mentions in AI answers · [scope]",
      "rows": [
        {
          "at": "b1",
          "label": "[brand]",
          "v": 50,
          "text": "50"
        },
        {
          "at": "b1",
          "label": "[brand]",
          "v": 20,
          "text": "20"
        },
        {
          "at": "b2",
          "label": "Nearest competitor",
          "v": 45,
          "text": "45",
          "muted": true
        }
      ],
      "foot": "[what the bars add up to]",
      "narration": "{b1}[The lead, by brand.] {b2}[Against the nearest competitor.] {foot}[What follows.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "p-win",
      "type": "title",
      "duration": 3,
      "kicker": "Job 3 of 3",
      "title": "Win what <em>others hold</em>",
      "sub": "[theme]: [why]"
    },
    {
      "id": "win",
      "type": "stats",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "Held by others · [topic]",
      "stats": [
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "AI prompts a month on [topic]"
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "competitors named there"
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "mentions of the firm, which publishes [its study]"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "[The topic.] {s1}[Demand.] {s2}[Who is named.] {s3}[The firm is not, though it has the material.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "win-how",
      "type": "browser",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "page": "finding",
          "url": "/research/annual-study/finding",
          "label": "<b>Research</b> a finding that names its source"
        }
      ],
      "rings": [
        {
          "at": "claim",
          "until": "cite",
          "mark": "finding.claim"
        },
        {
          "at": "cite",
          "mark": "finding.cite"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "So write the finding the other way round. {claim}One sentence that names the firm and the report. {cite}[How to cite it.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "human",
      "type": "stats",
      "hold": 0.4,
      "title": "The human side · [page], [views] views in [period]",
      "stats": [
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "n": "[n]%",
          "t": "of views click nothing"
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "n": "[n]%",
          "t": "from [source] click nothing ([share] of views)"
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "n": "[n]%",
          "t": "from [source] click nothing ([share] of views)"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "That is the visibility plan. The other half is what happens when a person arrives. {s1}[Share that clicks nothing.] {s2}[The worst source.] {s3}[The best.] One page, very different visitors."
    },
    {
      "id": "cohorts",
      "type": "strip",
      "hold": 0.6,
      "stagger": 0.18,
      "height": 800,
      "title": "One homepage, a version for each visitor",
      "sub": "Each a full page · sized on [page], [period]",
      "pages": [
        {
          "page": "c-default",
          "label": "No signal",
          "share": "[share]"
        },
        {
          "page": "c-search",
          "label": "Searched a product",
          "share": "[share]"
        },
        {
          "page": "c-answer",
          "label": "From an assistant",
          "share": "[share]"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "So the homepage has a version for each of them. {slots}The frame marks what changes first. [Two versions, one sentence each.] {pan}[The rest.] {end}Each version is sized on real traffic, and judged the way a person judges a page: did I find my reason to stay?"
    },
    {
      "id": "measure",
      "type": "stats",
      "hold": 0.3,
      "title": "One line to track it",
      "stats": [
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "topics owned, of [n] in the plan"
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "mentions and citations a month"
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "n": "[n]",
          "t": "AI-referred visits, and the leads they become"
        }
      ],
      "narration": "Last, how to know it works. One line: topics owned, mentions, citations, visits, leads. {s1}[Today.] {s2}[Today.] {s3}[Today.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "close",
      "type": "title",
      "hold": 1.0,
      "kicker": "Brand Visibility",
      "title": "Three reads.<br>One plan.<br><em>One experience.</em>",
      "sub": "Who arrives, what people ask and what the firm wants, merged by client theme. [Period and sources]: a starting point.",
      "narration": "So that's the model. Brand visibility isn't search, or AI, or the website. It's three reads of the same firm, merged into one plan, and one experience that carries it out."
    }
  ],
  "css": "deck-extras.css"
}
